bug_report:
[12/13/14/15/16 Regression] missing tail call to self with struct in some cases
Extracted fromhttps://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=92474#c1:
starting withr273603(r10-1982-g4eb503965ac70e), the trunk doesn't tail call optimize this either even without -fsanitize=, unless -fno-tree-sra.

testcase:
```
    struct MyStruct {
        unsigned  n_recurses;
    };

    MyStruct foo(MyStruct m) {
        return (m.n_recurses == 0)? m : foo(MyStruct{m.n_recurses - 1});
    }

    int main() {
        foo(MyStruct{999999});
    }
```
